00:08:09.823 --> 00:08:13.036
- As a startup founder how do
you maintain a positivity and a

00:08:13.036 --> 00:08:15.695
healthy culture through the
different stages of growth

00:08:15.695 --> 00:08:17.664
especially when it's
fast-paced growth?

00:08:17.664 --> 00:08:21.968
- Vayner went from 30 to 650
people in four years and from

00:08:21.968 --> 00:08:27.574
one to five offices including
London and the way I've kept

00:08:27.574 --> 00:08:28.908
culture is dictatorship.

00:08:28.908 --> 00:08:33.623
(audience laughter)

00:08:35.673 --> 00:08:39.914
It's just the thing that 
I care about the most.

00:08:39.914 --> 00:08:42.725
Here's how you keep culture when
Kristin in the office is upset

00:08:42.725 --> 00:08:45.358
about something and I'm on my
way from Connecticut in to

00:08:45.358 --> 00:08:47.465
New York to do a new business 
pitch potentially worth

00:08:47.465 --> 00:08:52.153
$5 million and I detour 
and skip that pitch to

00:08:52.153 --> 00:08:55.073
go and talk out 
with her that issue,

00:08:55.073 --> 00:08:57.337
that's how you maintain culture.

00:08:57.337 --> 00:08:59.973
Guys, life's very simple.

00:08:59.973 --> 00:09:02.509
There's the things you wish you
were doing, there's the things

00:09:02.509 --> 00:09:04.188
you're saying that 
you're doing and

00:09:04.188 --> 00:09:07.046
then there's the things 
that you actually do.

00:09:07.046 --> 00:09:10.150
The way you maintain culture is
the same answer as the question

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:11.384
prior to this.

00:09:11.384 --> 00:09:14.054
You do it in your actions.

00:09:14.054 --> 00:09:16.790
I don't meet with every single
employee that works for me for

00:09:16.790 --> 00:09:20.660
10 minutes three months in to
check the box and seem like a

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:22.195
personal CEO.

00:09:22.195 --> 00:09:25.065
