margin mainly because we think
we're going to get it all at the

00:11:54.147 --> 00:11:55.348
end of the day.

00:11:55.348 --> 00:11:58.084
Making 8% percent margin on 
$400 million is a hell of a lot more

00:11:58.084 --> 00:12:00.988
interesting than making 
20% on $30 million and

00:12:00.988 --> 00:12:02.255
so I'm playing the long game.

00:12:02.255 --> 00:12:03.389
I always have.

00:12:03.389 --> 00:12:05.525
It's why a lot of you have
good relationships with me.

00:12:05.525 --> 00:12:08.328
I see you at different places,
I know who you are, I care,

00:12:08.328 --> 00:12:10.296
I interact with you.

00:12:10.296 --> 00:12:12.727
Life is simple.

00:12:12.727 --> 00:12:13.705
The truth wins.

00:12:13.705 --> 00:12:16.069
You may be confused 'cause
times are tough and the media

00:12:16.069 --> 00:12:18.104
and there's always issues in
this country and we got flaws

00:12:18.104 --> 00:12:19.906
and all that stuff.

00:12:19.906 --> 00:12:22.642
You're more than welcome to
look at a pessimistic aspect of

00:12:22.642 --> 00:12:24.210
society and life.

00:12:24.210 --> 00:12:29.048
I choose to in my 80, 90 years
hopefully on earth to understand

00:12:29.048 --> 00:12:32.251
that I got to be a human being
which if you want to talk about

00:12:32.251 --> 00:12:34.045
big data and math the rarity of

00:12:34.045 --> 00:12:36.856
actually becoming 
a person is insane.

00:12:36.856 --> 00:12:40.526
And just way too many
people don't understand that and

00:12:40.526 --> 00:12:43.620
appreciate it and I do and so
I'm playing the long game

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:45.064
on all this stuff.

00:12:45.064 --> 00:12:46.199
- We're pretty lucky.

00:12:46.199 --> 00:12:46.866
Pretty lucky.

00:12:46.866 --> 00:12:47.900
- Super lucky.

00:12:47.900 --> 00:12:49.669
And you live in America?

00:12:49.669 --> 00:12:50.436
- Yeah.

00:12:50.436 --> 00:12:53.036
- You could have
been a rhinoceros.

00:12:53.036 --> 00:12:55.284
(audience laughter)

00:12:55.284 --> 00:12:59.012
Or like a tree. 
Fucking tree.

00:12:59.012 --> 00:13:03.750
Next question from Dan
(inaudible) another local

00:13:03.750 --> 00:13:05.284
success story.

00:13:05.284 --> 00:13:08.721
On CNBC's "Follow The Leader"
you said nobody outworks me.

00:13:08.721 --> 00:13:09.656
- I really believe that.

00:13:09.656 --> 00:13:10.823
- I do too.

00:13:10.823 --> 00:13:14.427
- How do you maintain that
without exhausting or killing

00:13:14.427 --> 00:13:15.995
all of those around you?

00:13:15.995 --> 00:13:17.363
- Oh, that's a great question.

00:13:17.363 --> 00:13:19.365
Overcommunitcating.

00:13:20.266 --> 00:13:21.668
It just comes to communication.

00:13:21.668 --> 00:13:24.771
I have to talk
with Lizzie a lot.

00:13:24.771 --> 00:13:26.406
The kids are getting older.

00:13:26.406 --> 00:13:30.543
I do think, I do think this will
be I'm getting into the end of

00:13:30.543 --> 00:13:33.613
an era like 17 and 18 hour
days because my children are now

00:13:33.613 --> 00:13:36.783
seven and four and they're just
more stuff that comes along with

00:13:36.783 --> 00:13:41.378
that so I think that's 
fine and that's great

00:13:41.378 --> 00:13:43.156
but it comes down 
to communication.

00:13:43.156 --> 00:13:45.892
I think people talk about work
life balance a lot, ever since I

00:13:45.892 --> 00:13:49.729
started doing DailyVee, which is
my video vlog daily kind of vlog

00:13:49.729 --> 00:13:53.099
thing, and Snapchat I think
a lot of you have followed me

00:13:53.099 --> 00:13:56.602
for several years have started
really realizing I wasn't joking

00:13:56.602 --> 00:13:58.071
that I was working this much.

00:13:58.071 --> 00:14:00.940
I think prior when I would talk
about hustle I think people were

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:03.776
like yeah he works hard but when
you get to see that it's fully

00:14:03.776 --> 00:14:07.280
documented and there's no
cheating and I'm working 7 AM to

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:11.584
midnight every single day, every
single day, every single minute

00:14:11.584 --> 00:14:12.652
it becomes intimidating.

00:14:12.652 --> 00:14:16.164
It's my natural just like some
of your some of very smart and

00:14:16.164 --> 00:14:19.627
some of you are very pretty and
some of you are very funny

00:14:19.627 --> 00:14:22.895
it's my natural state to
hustle that hard.

00:14:22.895 --> 00:14:26.730
Not being born this country,
coming up with nothing,

00:14:26.730 --> 00:14:29.235
feeling guilty that you have 
certain talents, there's a million

00:14:29.235 --> 00:14:31.233
reasons that it drives me.

00:14:31.233 --> 00:14:33.863
But what I love about 
this question is

00:14:33.863 --> 00:14:34.974
it's not how do I do it

00:14:34.974 --> 00:14:37.810
it's how do I keep the people
around me in a healthy place.

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:38.711
- And how does that happen?

00:14:38.711 --> 00:14:40.813
- It's a super
intense thing, man.

00:14:40.813 --> 00:14:43.429
I never judge
anybody's work life balance.

00:14:43.429 --> 00:14:45.518
As a matter of fact here's a
good opportunity for me,

00:14:45.518 --> 00:14:46.751
I always want to clear this up,

00:14:46.751 --> 00:14:48.988
I don't think you 
should work 15 hours a day.

00:14:48.988 --> 00:14:52.183
I think if you're, here's my
punchline if you're complaining

00:14:52.183 --> 00:14:54.947
about your life, you need to
look at what you're doing.

00:14:54.947 --> 00:14:57.098
So for example, I have friends
that are making hundreds of

00:14:57.098 --> 00:14:58.963
millions of dollars in their
careers and tens of million

00:14:58.963 --> 00:15:01.278
dollars a year and they're
complaining that they're not

00:15:01.278 --> 00:15:03.376
spending enough 
time with their family,

00:15:03.376 --> 00:15:05.694
then spend time 
with your family, dick.

00:15:05.694 --> 00:15:09.941
(applause and laughter)

00:15:09.941 --> 00:15:11.911
And then I have people 
emailing me every

00:15:11.911 --> 00:15:14.213
day complaining that their
business is not taking off and

00:15:14.213 --> 00:15:18.084
I go do one quick Twitter
search and they're 6 PM tweet is

00:15:18.084 --> 00:15:21.387
hitting the links
with my buddies.

00:15:21.387 --> 00:15:25.024
You're not going to win and
build a big business if you're

00:15:25.024 --> 00:15:29.495
watching "Game of Thrones" and
playing Pokémon Go all day.

00:15:29.495 --> 00:15:31.898
Nobody's won on just talent.

00:15:31.898 --> 00:15:34.801
Hard work is part
of the equation.

00:15:34.801 --> 00:15:36.169
I don't judge anybody.

00:15:36.169 --> 00:15:38.905
I think I get judged 'cause 
I put myself out there and then

00:15:38.905 --> 00:15:41.407
I deserve to be judged and when
people hit me up and say

00:15:41.407 --> 00:15:43.369
you're gonna regret this, 
you're gonna regret this

00:15:43.369 --> 00:15:45.327
and I get that.
I get those emails.

00:15:45.327 --> 00:15:48.414
I reply all the time, I'm
like you don't know me.

00:15:48.414 --> 00:15:51.818
I respect why you're saying that
because one thing that some of

00:15:51.818 --> 00:15:54.587
you who really follow me know is
my wife and I have decided not

00:15:54.587 --> 00:15:56.556
to share our
family life on social.

00:15:56.556 --> 00:15:59.458
So unlike a lot of my tech
friends who use the cute

00:15:59.458 --> 00:16:02.028
pictures of their kids to
get more likes on their social

00:16:02.028 --> 00:16:05.164
media, I'm not interested in
doing that with my children.

00:16:05.164 --> 00:16:06.465
I'm going to let them decide.

00:16:06.465 --> 00:16:08.088
Misha's already, I think 
she's gonna have a

00:16:08.088 --> 00:16:09.435
YouTube show in a week.

00:16:09.435 --> 00:16:12.371
It seems like she
wants to do that, great.

00:16:12.371 --> 00:16:15.775
But I don't want to do that and
so it feels even more extreme,

00:16:15.775 --> 00:16:16.475
right?

00:16:16.475 --> 00:16:19.779
I always ask people that really
call me out on it I'm like if

00:16:19.779 --> 00:16:21.814
